# Qualcomm SM8350 shared kernel settings.
#
# What belongs here is what is true of the chip; what is true of one board
# belongs in that board's defconfig. The two are separated because a value
# lifted from a sibling phone into the SoC layer breaks every other board
# using it.

# ---- Platform ------------------------------------------------------------
# GICv3 distributor 0x17a00000, redistributor 0x17a60000 stride 0x20000,
# 4 interrupt cells in the ADT encoding. 19.2 MHz always-on XO.
# CONFIG_XNU_ARM_DT_PLATFORM and CONFIG_XNU_ARMCPU are selected by the board:
# a board that does not want a CPU driver still wants the DTS parser.

# ---- Storage -------------------------------------------------------------
# ufshc@1d84000 with ufs_ice@1d88000 and ufs_ice_hwkm@1d90000;
# the PHY is ufsphy_mem@1d87000 (0xe10), qcom,ufs-phy-qmp-v4-lahaina.
# The transport is a component (ShengUfs carries an SM8350 fork); whether a
# board enables it, and whether it builds probe-only, is the board's choice.
# CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_UFS is left to the board defconfig.

# ---- GPU -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Adreno 660 on SM8350 is chipid 0x06060001. UniXNU's Adreno740 and
# AdrenoMetal target A740 + SM8550 interfaces only; nothing in the catalog
# drives an A660 today. The registers are described in this layer's DTSI so
# that a driver has a target, but no configuration selects one.
# CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_ADRENO is not set

# ---- Display -------------------------------------------------------------
# mdss_mdp@ae00000 (0x84000) + vbif (0x2008) + regdma (0x800); SPI 0x53.
# dsi_ctrl0@ae94000 / dsi_phy0@ae94400, dsi_ctrl1@ae96000 / dsi_phy1@ae96400.
# Six CTLs, six mixers, four DSPPs. No native display driver for this SoC
# exists in the catalog; a board uses the loader's frame buffer until one does.

# ---- PCIe ----------------------------------------------------------------
# pcie@1c00000 (parf 0x3000, phy 0x2000, dm_core at 0x60000000, elbi, iatu,
# conf 0x100000), smmu-sid-base 0x1c00, TBU 0x151a1000. This is the bus the
# WCN6855-family radio sits on. No transport is implemented yet.
# CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_WIFI is not set

# ---- Power ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PM8350 + PMK8350 over the SPMI arbiter; 65 thermal zones on a live phone.
# CONFIG_XNU_SHENG_PMGR supplies the PMGR call site the platform code expects.
